<% content_for(:html_title, 'Electronic Records and Signature Disclosure | Evergentic eSign') %>
<main class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-10 prose" id="main">
  <h1>Electronic Records and Signature Disclosure</h1>
  <p>Evergentic (Specialty Management Services LLC d/b/a Evergentic) uses Evergentic eSign to send documents for electronic signature. Please read this disclosure before you sign.</p>
  <h2>Your consent</h2>
  <p>By choosing to sign electronically, you agree to receive and sign the document, and the records related to it, in electronic form, and you agree that your electronic signature is the legal equivalent of your handwritten signature (U.S. ESIGN Act, 15 U.S.C. &sect; 7001 et seq.; Florida Uniform Electronic Transaction Act, Fla. Stat. &sect; 668.50).</p>
  <h2>Paper copies and withdrawing consent</h2>
  <p>You may ask for a paper copy of any document you signed, at no charge, and you may withdraw your consent to electronic records at any time before you sign, by writing to the Evergentic person who sent you the document, or to <a href="mailto:hello@evergentic.ai">hello@evergentic.ai</a>. Withdrawing consent does not affect documents already signed. If you withdraw, we will send documents on paper instead.</p>
  <h2>What you need</h2>
  <p>A current web browser (recent Chrome, Edge, Safari or Firefox), an email address that can receive messages, and a way to view and keep PDF files. After signing you can download the signed document and its audit trail; we also email you a copy. Tell us if your email address changes.</p>
  <h2>Records we keep</h2>
  <p>We keep the signed document and an audit trail (signing events, times, IP address and browser) as described in our <a href="https://evergentic.ai/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and our <a href="https://evergentic.ai/legal/data-retention">Data Retention and Disposal Policy</a>.</p>
</main>
